WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.060 --> 00:00:05.509
Hey youtubers it's Charlie and this week on
Orphan Black it's all about blowing shit up.

00:00:05.509 --> 00:00:10.940
Mrs S and Sarah divide and conquer and Vic
the Dick gets molested by elves. Not really,

00:00:10.940 --> 00:00:15.690
but we get to see some amazing Tatiana Maslany
acting as Sarah acting as another clone. We

00:00:15.690 --> 00:00:20.109
also got to meet Michelle Forbes. She's playing
Rachel's boss at the Dyad.

00:00:20.109 --> 00:00:23.150
If you're finding me for the first time I
try to do Orphan Black videos every week.

00:00:23.150 --> 00:00:26.669
Be sure to subscribe to get everything. I'm
down about two episodes just because I was

00:00:26.669 --> 00:00:29.769
out of town but there's links to the full
playlist in the description.

00:00:29.769 --> 00:00:33.620
So let's talk about how crazy things are getting.
Careful for spoilers in case you haven't seen

00:00:33.620 --> 00:00:38.340
the episode. Here's my top 5 wtf moments,
then I'll do my review. Number 5 - Vic the

00:00:38.340 --> 00:00:40.890
Dick gets molested by elves.

00:00:40.890 --> 00:00:45.800
We need a book of Felix quotes. I think of
him as the punch up guy. Like when Allison

00:00:45.800 --> 00:00:50.230
and Sarah just get way to heavy he just pokes
his head into frame and says something crazy.

00:00:50.230 --> 00:00:53.700
Vic was totally a dick though. He deserved
everything that happened to him. The whole

00:00:53.700 --> 00:00:59.280
Vic Sarah shitstorm wasn't quite as funny
as I expected it to be. Just painfully awkward.

00:00:59.280 --> 00:01:04.030
I was surprised to find out that the police
officer he was talking to was the same one

00:01:04.030 --> 00:01:11.030
who tried to get information out of Allison
in the parking lot a couple of episodes ago.

00:01:11.960 --> 00:01:14.689
Number 4 - Sarah Pretends To Be Allison

00:01:14.689 --> 00:01:20.170
I always love watching Tatiana do clones acting
as other clones. I don't know why she hasn't

00:01:20.170 --> 00:01:25.149
won an emmy for it yet. The minute she started
dropping Monitor bombs on Donnie during their

00:01:25.149 --> 00:01:29.259
role playing session I knew he was going to
figure everything out soon. To be fair Allison

00:01:29.259 --> 00:01:33.950
had to explain it to him, but we finally get
a peek inside Donnie's head.

00:01:33.950 --> 00:01:39.240
I actually expected him to be like any other
monitor but turns out Leekie was playing him

00:01:39.240 --> 00:01:42.350
for the fool the whole time. It is kind of
sweet to think that he was being genuine the

00:01:42.350 --> 00:01:44.929
whole time. He just thought it was some low
grade social experiment. That kind of explains

00:01:44.929 --> 00:01:46.639
why he's so terrible at the spy stuff.

00:01:46.639 --> 00:01:52.359
I think all of this means there's a good chance
he could wind up switching sides so to speak

00:01:52.359 --> 00:01:56.350
and helping Clone Club before the end of the
season. He's like the loveable goofball of

00:01:56.350 --> 00:01:59.090
the show, so that's why that surprise at the
end was so shocking. I'll talk about that

00:01:59.090 --> 00:01:59.399
in a sec.

00:01:59.399 --> 00:02:02.189
Number 3 - Rachel Confronts Doctor Leekie

00:02:02.189 --> 00:02:06.359
Mrs S and Sarah blow their shit up. It worked,
not quite as expected and there was the added

00:02:06.359 --> 00:02:13.359
twist of Rachel's boss Michelle Forbes, siding
with her over Leekie. They'd kind of teased

00:02:15.730 --> 00:02:22.340
Leekie's side projects. Like the artificial
womb was just the tip of the iceberg. I'm

00:02:22.340 --> 00:02:26.110
hoping they uncover more of his secret research
later in the season.

00:02:26.110 --> 00:02:31.629
There is so much going on inside of Dyad right
now, it's like King's Landing in Game of Thrones.

00:02:31.629 --> 00:02:33.879
They're all liars.

00:02:33.879 --> 00:02:38.780
Rachel did defy Marion's wishes and let Leekie
go, which suggests that she might do something

00:02:38.780 --> 00:02:43.250
to help the clones against Marion's wishes
before the finale. Michelle Forbes actually

00:02:43.250 --> 00:02:48.400
did an interview about her character. She
teased that in the last two episodes of the

00:02:48.400 --> 00:02:54.610
season Marion gets progressively weirder.
And she's the kind of person who's so powerful,

00:02:54.610 --> 00:02:58.209
it doesn't even occur to her that subordinates
like Rachel would defy her.

00:02:58.209 --> 00:03:03.659
She's really complex, but I see her more than
Rachel being the ultimate antagonist this

00:03:03.659 --> 00:03:08.379
season. Don't be surprised if Rachel becomes
a stealth Clone Club member.

00:03:08.379 --> 00:03:11.180
Number 2 - Kira Stem Cells

00:03:11.180 --> 00:03:17.439
This was one of the few major violations in
the episode. In case you're confused. Leekie

00:03:17.439 --> 00:03:22.420
and Delphine harvested Kira's stem cells from
a tooth she lost a long time ago. It's really

00:03:22.420 --> 00:03:29.000
small, so there's not a lot. They used those
stem cells to treat Cosima, without her knowledge.

00:03:29.000 --> 00:03:36.000
They totally worked, but that's not the issue.
Cosima is totally right to flip out. Delphine

00:03:38.299 --> 00:03:44.969
almost seemed like a mad scientist during
their shouting match. But in the end she still

00:03:44.969 --> 00:03:49.859
needs more of Kira's stem cells or she'll
die. Even the teaser for the next episode

00:03:49.859 --> 00:03:51.879
shows her spitting up blood.

00:03:51.879 --> 00:03:57.840
It seems like as we get closer to the finale,
events are conspiring to bring everyone back

00:03:57.840 --> 00:04:03.859
together. Sarah is coming back with Kira nd
Donnie and Allison start discussing the Dyad

00:04:03.859 --> 00:04:05.359
experiment.

00:04:05.359 --> 00:04:12.359
I can't wait to see how Michelle Forbes character
pulls the strings to get them all to dance.

00:04:13.829 --> 00:04:17.319
Number 1 - Donnie Kills Doctor Leekie

00:04:17.319 --> 00:04:22.210
I love how casually this scene started out.
Leekie doesn't even care to give Donnie the

00:04:22.210 --> 00:04:27.979
time of day, he's a speck of dust in the grand
design. But all it takes is one random encounter

00:04:27.979 --> 00:04:32.569
to blow everything up. In this case, literally
Leekie's head.

00:04:32.569 --> 00:04:36.830
It is confirmed, unless there is a Leekie
Clone floating around somewhere, he's gone

00:04:36.830 --> 00:04:42.289
for good. But his influence will still inform
some really important things. That artificial

00:04:42.289 --> 00:04:45.430
womb he was talking about. That's probably
going to have something to do with Cosima

00:04:45.430 --> 00:04:52.430
getting better. That camera footage during
her operation was from inside her womb. She's

00:04:52.680 --> 00:04:55.410
full of cancer, that's what the stem cells
are treating.

00:04:55.410 --> 00:05:00.060
But I'm really interested to see if Cosima
and Delphine hijack Leekie's secret projects

00:05:00.060 --> 00:05:03.110
to help solve the problem.

00:05:03.110 --> 00:05:07.669
But now it's your turn, let me know what your
favorite moment was? Donnie Killing Leekie,

00:05:07.669 --> 00:05:13.400
Sarah's Speech as Allison or Vic the Dick?

00:05:13.400 --> 00:05:17.090
Overall I gave the episode a B plus. As complex
as the show already is, I feel like they're

00:05:17.090 --> 00:05:21.789
doing a great job of escalating everything.
I was bummed we didn't catch up with Helena

00:05:21.789 --> 00:05:27.479
this week, but I don't expect them to be able
to fit everyone into every episode.

00:05:27.479 --> 00:05:31.150
Leekie as a character is irreplaceable. But
I think the show is trading the Mad Scientist

00:05:31.150 --> 00:05:37.130
for The Smoking Man. Right now I think of
Michelle Forbes' character as being like the

00:05:37.130 --> 00:05:42.340
Smoking Man from X-Files. Controlling everything
from a distance and totally ruthless in sticking

00:05:42.340 --> 00:05:44.440
to an ominous plan.

00:05:44.440 --> 00:05:49.500
Michelle Forbes is a neolutionist, so obviously
her goal is to patent human beings eventually.

00:05:49.500 --> 00:05:52.569
As opposed to the Proletheans that just want
to homogenize the world.

00:05:52.569 --> 00:05:57.620
One of my favorite things about the show and
something this episode did really well was

00:05:57.620 --> 00:06:02.770
give characters a very grand send off. Like
the producers say, we're going to kill you.

00:06:02.770 --> 00:06:08.030
But it's going to be amazing.

00:06:08.030 --> 00:06:11.770
Donnie sounds like he's on the run in the
next episode, but I think he's going to end

00:06:11.770 --> 00:06:16.710
up turning to Clone Club for help. I'm very
hopeful for his character. The only alternative

00:06:16.710 --> 00:06:22.770
is for the Dyad to hunt him down. Either they
will or Sarah will send Helena after him.

00:06:22.770 --> 00:06:27.289
The thing I'm looking forward to most right
now is learning more about the Marion character

00:06:27.289 --> 00:06:31.460
and seeing what happens when Sarah turns herself
and Kira into the Dyad. I'm also kind of wondering

00:06:31.460 --> 00:06:35.710
what Rachel is going to do with Duncan, eventually
they have to meet.

00:06:35.710 --> 00:06:41.639
So I'll be posting my next Orphan Black episode
next week after episode 8. Be sure to subscribe

00:06:41.639 --> 00:06:46.220
to get it. Also, if you have questions about
episode 6, the one I missed while I was away.

00:06:46.220 --> 00:06:48.259
Just leave them in the comments.

00:06:48.259 --> 00:06:52.949
Right now click here for my last Orphan Black
video and click here for my Maleficent Review.

00:06:52.949 --> 00:06:55.470
Thanks for watching, see you guys tomorrow
for fire and blood. High Fives!

